# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MovieMind — secrets
# The TMDb credential must never be committed. fetch_tmdb_snapshot.py reads it
# from the environment (TMDB_API_READ_ACCESS_TOKEN or TMDB_API_KEY).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
secrets/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MovieMind — raw dataset (NOT redistributable)
#
# The snapshot is fetched from the official TMDb API. TMDb's API Terms of Use
# grant free NON-COMMERCIAL use with mandatory attribution; they do NOT grant
# redistribution rights. Committing the snapshot to a public repository would
# be redistribution, so it is excluded from version control entirely.
#
# See docs/phase-02-dataset-audit.md for the full provenance analysis.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTE: the pattern must be `data/*` (not `data/`), because git does not descend
# into an excluded DIRECTORY, so a later `!data/.gitkeep` could never re-include
# the file. `data/*` excludes the contents while keeping the directory trackable.
data/*
!data/.gitkeep

# Belt-and-braces: never let these slip in even if a rule above is edited.
data/raw/
data/audit/
# Phase 3 derived features. Regenerable from data/raw/ by
# `python scripts/build_features.py`, and still derived from TMDb content, so
# it is not committable either.
data/processed/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Audit / build artifacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
reports/
*.log
audit_snapshot*.json
audit_report*.md
*.sqlite
*.db

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Node / frontend build output
#
# `frontend/.gitignore` also covers these, and a nested .gitignore does apply
# inside git. They are repeated here because they are the single largest things
# that could be staged by accident, and the root file is the one a reader opens
# first. `package-lock.json` is deliberately NOT ignored: it is what makes an
# `npm ci` reproducible.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/dist-ssr/
frontend/.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo
coverage/
.nyc_output/
# `public/` is the static directory the FastAPI preset serves, and it is pure
# build output: deploy/stage_frontend.py wipes and repopulates it from
# frontend/dist on every Vercel build. Committing it would mean committing a
# copy of the frontend bundle that goes stale on the next build.
/public/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deployment tooling
#
# `vercel.json` and `.python-version` ARE committed -- they are how the public
# repository reproduces the deployment, and neither contains a secret. What
# must never be committed is anything Vercel writes locally, or a corpus that
# arrived outside `data/`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vercel/
*.partial
# `vercel build` drops a ~54 MB `uv` binary in the repository root when it has to
# bootstrap one itself. It is a toolchain download, not source.
/_uv/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Temporary files
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.tmp
*.temp
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
*.log
~$*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS / editor noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

.vercel
.env*
